  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Electoral Reforms are promulgated strengthening electoral systems and processes.
Increased civic awareness and engagement with the electoral process
Enhanced cooperation and consultation between IEC and IPC.
Legal Drafting Unit established in the National Assembly
Capacities of selected committees are assessed and legislative roles strengthened
Capacities of selected CSOs and Media Houses assessed and strengthened.
Anti Corruption Agency is established and functional
A revised Constitution is approved</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2019">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">2016 Presidential elections.
95% of elected members in 2017 National Assembly elections are new.
Emerging tensions following presidential elections and political impasse.
Significant number of CSOs but under-resourced and lack strategic focus
Current(1997) Constitution amended several times to perpetuate former President&apos;s regime
No Anti Corruption Agency</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	Mobilization of funds to support the 2020-2022 electoral cycle ahead of promoting a credible, transparent and sustainable 2021 Political Engagement and Electoral Processes.
&#x2022;	Personnel of MDA and journalist training on the National Assembly rules of procedures (standing orders) and parliamentary reporting.
Procurement of Hansard equipment to strengthen the capacity of the National Assembly. 
&#x2022;	 Review the NA Strategic and Investment Plan in harmonization existing NA policies as well as develop the constitution, policies and guidelines for the Women Caucus.
&#x2022;	Gender Equality Seal integrated into 8 Private Sector Organisations in the Gambia.
&#x2022;	Raphella Gambia Chapter fully established and popularized in The Gambia.
&#x2022;	Establishment of the National Infrastructure for Peace (I4P)
&#x2022;	Adoption of the Gambian reviewed constitution
&#x2022;	Increase awareness of the Constitutional review and referendum process in the Gambia
&#x2022;	Institutional capacity of TANGO strengthened
&#x2022;	Increase awareness amongst citizens about Anti-Corruption and accountability mechanisms in the Gambia.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	Citizen&#x2019;s understanding of the content of the draft constitution ahead of the referendum across the country increased.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	National consultation on developing an institutional framework for the establishment of an I4P in The Gambia
&#x2022;	Conduct radio and TV programme to raise awareness on The Gambia Infrastructure for Peace
&#x2022;	Development of the Standard Operating Procedure for the Operationalization of The Gambia Infrastructure for Peace
&#x2022;	Formulation of a draft multi- year proposal on the operationalisation and implementation of The Gambia National Council for Peace and Social Cohesion.
&#x2022;	Hired a consultant to conduct a desk review The Gambia National Action Pan 2012 and develop The Gambia National Action Plan on United Nations Security Council Resolution 1325
&#x2022;	Development of a strategic and operational plan, guidelines, and implementation modalities on the autonomy of the National Assembly</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	Regional consultation on developing an institutional framework for the establishment of an I4P in The Gambia conducted.
&#x2022;	Draft multi- year proposal on the operationalization and implementation of The Gambia National Council for Peace and Social Cohesion and draft Standard Operating Procedure for the Operationalization of The Gambia Infrastructure for Peace produced.
&#x2022;	Draft desk review report on The Gambia National Action Pan 2012 and The Gambia National Action Plan on United Nations Security Council Resolution 1325 produced
&#x2022;	National Assembly Service Bill 2021 enacted.
&#x2022;	Three days retreat to develop the strategic and operational plan, guidelines, and implementation modalities on the autonomy of the National Assembly held.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
